-- title:
--   Function field of a descended model: F=F₀· L
-- statement:
--   Fix an algebraically closed field $L$ of universe $u$, a valuation subring $A\subseteq L$, a field $F$ with an $L$-algebra structure, index types $\iota_V,\iota_E$, and for each $i\in\iota_V$ a field $\overline{F}_i$ that is an algebra over the residue field of $A$. Fix component charts $C_i$ (each consisting of a valuation subring of $F$ with surjective residue map onto $\overline{F}_i$, a set of places of $F/L$, a finite set of nodal places of $\overline{F}_i$, a map of places and the stated compatibilities), annuli $\mathrm{An}_e$ in $F$ over $A$, maps $\mathrm{src},\mathrm{tgt}\colon\iota_E\to\iota_V$ and places $x_s(e)$, $x_t(e)$ of $\overline{F}_{\mathrm{src}(e)}$, $\overline{F}_{\mathrm{tgt}(e)}$ over the residue field of $A$. Let $M$ be a semistable model for this combinatorial datum: an integral scheme $X$, proper, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, together with an isomorphism $F\cong K(X)$ compatible with the constants $A$, points of $X$ attached to places, to the $i$ and to the charts' smooth and nodal points, and the bijectivity and specialisation axioms of the structure (summarised here). Let $D$ be a descent of $M$: a Noetherian Henselian local ring $A_0$ with an injective local homomorphism $\iota\colon A_0\to A$, a subfield $K_0\subseteq L$ with $\iota(A_0)=A\cap K_0$ and $L$ algebraic over $K_0$, surjectivity of $A_0\to A/\mathfrak m_A$, an integral scheme $X_0$ proper, flat and locally of finite presentation over $\operatorname{Spec} A_0$, an isomorphism $M.X\cong X_0\times_{\operatorname{Spec} A_0}\operatorname{Spec} A$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$ carrying the generic point of $M.X$ to that of $X_0$, and a subfield $F_0\subseteq F$ with $F$ algebraic over $F_0$ together with an isomorphism $F_0\cong K(X_0)$ compatible with $F\cong K(X)$ through the stalk map at the generic point. Then for every $s\in F$ there is a finite subset $\Lambda\subseteq L$ such that $s$ lies in the subfield of $F$ generated by $F_0$ together with the image of $\Lambda$ under $\operatorname{algebraMap} L F$.
--
--   This records that the function field of a semistable model obtained by base change from a model over $A_0$ is the compositum $F_0\cdot L$ of the descended function field and the constants, in the pointwise form that each element of $F$ already lies in $F_0$ adjoined finitely many constants. It is used when a finite set of functions on the model has to be defined over a finitely generated level, and is cited by the two results on membership in principal divisor groups for descended semistable models.
